    {"name": "Base-Drag Hack Transition", "type": "Transition", "id": "67405a47-2e95-4e1b-b99c-14f0ab3020d8", "comment": "Because this example has a length to diameter ratio of less than a 10:1, additional base drag should be generated for this rocket. In this instance, to apply additional base drag, affix a transition to the bottom of the rocket, set the fore-diameter to .001 in., the aft-diameter to 3 in., and the length to pi * 3 (9.425 in.). Now, check the three boxes that override the mass, center of gravity, and coefficient of drag of the base drag transition.", "objGroup": "15_Base-Drag Hack Transition", "length": 0.24745949999999997, "instanceCount": 1, "locations": [[0.16656538461538462, 0.0, 0.0]], "componentMass": 9.443612462921172E-4, "componentVolume": 7.86967705243431E-7, "materialDensity": 1200.0, "materialType": "Bulk"}
